I decided to try foodless out. Naturally I chose to play a monk. Since
I had broke weaponless with a pick-axe in my two monk ascensions I was
going to keep that intact as well.

The early game was fairly ordinary, except the whole praying every ~800
turns deal. Minetown was coaligned so I could take the edge off my
prayer timeout by sacrifice (but not sacrificing excessively so my god
gives me gifts while I starve).

Sokoban held a bag of holding, but the real treasure was a ring of slow
digestion, which I price-IDed then, seeing that it was in the
appropriate price group, sink-IDed. Soon after I got a fountain wish
(beefy monks can take out damn near anything) by dipping a useless item
into fountains. I chose the Eye of the Aethiopica because I enjoy
having MR that doesn't take up an equipment slot. The power
regeneration, telepathy, and branchporting are just delicious icing on
the cake.

I had plenty of scrolls of enchant armor. Enchanted my robe up, as it
was the only piece of equipment I was planning on keeping post-Castle.
Coupled with donation (deep leprechaun hall gave me ~$12000) and
wear-testing everything I could find, my AC was -9. Not at all bad for
a pre-Castle Monk.

Some other lovely sights: tons of stores, including a largish tool
shop. Got *two* magic markers and a can of grease. A few good spells,
all at 0% fail. Started with sleep and learned magic missile. I knew
detect monsters but I used the Eye plus a towel because that uses far
less nutrition (most of the time, none). Found a luckstone the level
below Minetown, quickly maxed out my luck through the two gray unicorns
(and the altar) on Minetown. I also had just about everything I was
carrying identified.

Really, the only thing I was lacking was reflection. I was going to
spend a wish
at the Castle for an amulet of reflection.

Hell, this is starting to read like a YAAP.

But it's not. On dungeon level 21 I ran into a floating eye. A floating
eye which my grand-master-in-martial-arts hit did not take down. A
floating eye which paralyzed me while a captain ambled over and shoved
his silver saber down my throat. I was hoping -9 AC and 87 HP would be
able to survive the captain but nay.

I am very disappointed because this kind of wonderful start only comes
once every couple hundred games. Since it's dungeon level 21, chances
are someone on nethack.alt.org will find a very lovely bones pile.

